From: Alex Scotti <alexscotti@gmail.com>
Subject: video: frame-packed MVC - VD1 stops at the end of its own eye

3D Blu-ray MVC played as HDMI frame packing on an AM9 Pro (S6) showed the left
eye on top, a green band where the active space is, and black where the right
eye belongs. Both views do reach the video layer: the MVC frame's view 0 goes
to VD1 and view 1 to VD2 (both MIFs enabled, reading different buffers - the
captured buffers are the same instant with depth-dependent horizontal
parallax), VD2_BLEND_SRC_CTRL routes VD2 into the preblend (0x2), and VD2's
window is the lower eye slot (lines 1125..2204 of 1920x2205).

What hides it is VD1's preblend window. config_vd_blend() does compute an MVC
window, then unconditionally overwrites it with the generic one - the post
blend span, or 0..VPP_PREBLEND_VD_V_END_LIMIT-1 (read back as 0x8FF = 2303) -
and its 3D fix-up only handles MODE_3D_OUT_TB and MODE_3D_OUT_LR, not frame
packing. So VD1, whose picture is 1080 lines, owns the whole packed frame and
its empty area covers VD2.

Writing VPP_PREBLEND_VD1_V_START_END (0x1d1b) to 0..1079 by hand during
playback made the right eye appear. Do that in config_vd_blend() for an MVC
frame under framepacking_support, from the eye height the decoder records
(left_eye.height), so the window follows the stream rather than a constant.

Top/bottom and side-by-side output are untouched; they also showed one eye on
this box and are not fixed by this.
---
--- a/drivers/media/video_sink/video_hw.c
+++ b/drivers/media/video_sink/video_hw.c
@@ -6339,6 +6339,20 @@
 				cur_frame_par->VPP_vd_start_lines_;
 			setting->preblend_v_end =
 				cur_frame_par->VPP_vd_end_lines_;
+		} else if (dispbuf && (dispbuf->type & VIDTYPE_MVC) &&
+			   framepacking_support &&
+			   dispbuf->left_eye.height) {
+			/*
+			 * Frame packing: VD1 carries the left eye only, VD2 the
+			 * right eye in the lower slot of the packed frame. The
+			 * generic preblend window above spans the whole packed
+			 * frame (0..VPP_PREBLEND_VD_V_END_LIMIT-1), so VD1's
+			 * empty area covers VD2: one eye, a green active-space
+			 * band, black below. Stop VD1 at the end of its eye.
+			 */
+			setting->preblend_v_start = 0;
+			setting->preblend_v_end =
+				dispbuf->left_eye.height - 1;
 		}
 	}
 #endif
